sentences.t:
Ille, ut opes fractae Teucrum, et Fortuna recessit,
res Agamemnonias victriciaque arma secutus,
fas omne abrumpit;

sentences.l:
He, when the resources broken of the Teucrians, and Fortune withdrew,
the Agamemnonian cause and victorious arms following,
all right breaks through;

sentences.t:
stant Manibus arae,
caeruleis maestae vittis atraque cupresso,
et circum Iliades crinem de more solutae;

sentences.l:
stand to the Shades altars,
dark-blue mournful with fillets and black with cypress,
and around the Ilian women, their hair according to custom loosed;

sentences.t:
Rex Anius, rex idem hominum Phoebique sacerdos
vittis et sacra redimitus tempora lauro,
occurrit;

sentences.l:
King Anius, king too of men and of Phoebus priest,
with fillets and holy bound as to the temples with laurel,
meets us;
